## 1. `DefaultExcerptGenerator` inner class

**PostReconciler** lines 430–437 / **SinglePageReconciler** lines 412–419.

**Differences: NONE.** The bodies are byte-for-byte identical:
```java
static class DefaultExcerptGenerator implements ExcerptGenerator {
    @Override
    public Mono<String> generate(Context context) {
        String shortHtmlContent = ExcerptUtils.substringByCodePoints(context.getContent(), 500);
        String text = Jsoup.parse(shortHtmlContent).text();
        return Mono.just(ExcerptUtils.substringByCodePoints(text, 150));
    }
}
```
**Feasibility: trivial** — extract to a package-level `DefaultExcerptGenerator` class in `run.halo.app.core.reconciler`; both reconcilers reference it. No parameters needed.

---

## 2. `listSnapshots`

**PostReconciler** lines 439–444 / **SinglePageReconciler** lines 426–431.

**Differences: NONE.** Both are:
```java
List<Snapshot> listSnapshots(Ref ref) {
    var snapshotListOptions = new ListOptions();
    snapshotListOptions.setFieldSelector(
            FieldSelector.of(Queries.equal("spec.subjectRef", Snapshot.toSubjectRefKey(ref))));
    return client.listAll(Snapshot.class, snapshotListOptions, Sort.unsorted());
}
```
**Feasibility: trivial** — move to an abstract base class or a shared static utility taking `ExtensionClient`.

---

## 3. `cleanUpResources`

**PostReconciler** lines 349–361:
```java
private void cleanUpResources(Post post) {
    final Ref ref = Ref.of(post);
    listSnapshots(ref).forEach(client::delete);
    commentService.removeBySubject(ref).block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
    counterService
            .deleteByName(MeterUtils.nameOf(Post.class, post.getMetadata().getName()))
            .block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
}
```

**SinglePageReconciler** lines 246–259:
```java
private void cleanUpResources(SinglePage singlePage) {
    Ref ref = Ref.of(singlePage);
    listSnapshots(ref).forEach(client::delete);
    commentService.removeBySubject(ref).block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
    counterService
            .deleteByName(MeterUtils.nameOf(
                    SinglePage.class, singlePage.getMetadata().getName()))
            .block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
}
```

**Differences:** Only the type token passed to `MeterUtils.nameOf()`:
- Post: `MeterUtils.nameOf(Post.class, post.getMetadata().getName())`
- SinglePage: `MeterUtils.nameOf(SinglePage.class, singlePage.getMetadata().getName())`

Both `Post` and `SinglePage` extend `AbstractExtension` (implement `Extension`), and `Ref.of()` takes an `Extension`.

**Feasibility: straightforward** — parameterize as `<T extends Extension> void cleanUpResources(Class<T> type, T extension)`. The single differing token becomes the `type` parameter. A base class can hold this method with `listSnapshots`, `commentService`, and `counterService`.

---

## 4. `subscribeNewCommentNotification`

**PostReconciler** lines 270–279:
```java
void subscribeNewCommentNotification(Post post) {
    var subscriber = new Subscription.Subscriber();
    subscriber.setName(post.getSpec().getOwner());
    var interestReason = new Subscription.InterestReason();
    interestReason.setReasonType(NotificationReasonConst.NEW_COMMENT_ON_POST);
    interestReason.setExpression(
            "props.postOwner == '%s'".formatted(post.getSpec().getOwner()));
    notificationCenter.subscribe(subscriber, interestReason).block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
}
```

**SinglePageReconciler** lines 108–117:
```java
void subscribeNewCommentNotification(SinglePage page) {
    var subscriber = new Subscription.Subscriber();
    subscriber.setName(page.getSpec().getOwner());
    var interestReason = new Subscription.InterestReason();
    interestReason.setReasonType(NotificationReasonConst.NEW_COMMENT_ON_PAGE);
    interestReason.setExpression(
            "props.pageOwner == '%s'".formatted(page.getSpec().getOwner()));
    notificationCenter.subscribe(subscriber, interestReason).block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
}
```

**Differences:**
- `NEW_COMMENT_ON_POST` vs `NEW_COMMENT_ON_PAGE`
- `"props.postOwner == '%s'"` vs `"props.pageOwner == '%s'"`

`getSpec().getOwner()` is present on both `Post.PostSpec` and `SinglePage.SinglePageSpec` but they don't share a common interface.

**Feasibility: straightforward** — extract a private helper taking `(String ownerName, String reasonType, String expressionTemplate)`:
```java
private void subscribeNewCommentNotification(
        String ownerName, String reasonType, String expressionTemplate) {
    var subscriber = new Subscription.Subscriber();
    subscriber.setName(ownerName);
    var interestReason = new Subscription.InterestReason();
    interestReason.setReasonType(reasonType);
    interestReason.setExpression(expressionTemplate.formatted(ownerName));
    notificationCenter.subscribe(subscriber, interestReason).block(BLOCKING_TIMEOUT);
}
```
Each reconciler keeps its own wrapper that supplies the constants. If extracted to a shared base, the caller passes the owner and the two string constants.

---

## 5. `getExcerpt` — partial duplication only

The checksum-caching skeleton is shared (~15 lines), but these lines differ materially and preclude a simple extraction:

| | PostReconciler | SinglePageReconciler |
|---|---|---|
| Content fetch | `postService.getContent(...)` | `singlePageService.getContent(...)` |
| Keywords | fetches tags, adds title | `Set.of()` (empty) |
| Context builder | `.setRawType(content.getRawType())` | `.setRaw(content.getRawType())` ← **apparent bug** (`.setRaw` instead of `.setRawType`) |
| Blank-content guard | `StringUtils.isAnyBlank(content.getContent(), content.getRaw())` present | absent |

Not a straightforward extraction; the `getExcerpt` duplication is better addressed by fixing the SinglePage bug (`.setRaw` → `.setRawType`) separately.

---

